<title>CANADA: Results of Canadian federal election.</title>
<headline>Results of Canadian federal election.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of</p>
<p>Monday's federal election among the five main parties, as</p>
<p>reported by the government agency Elections Canada:</p>
<p> PARTY	     SEATS  1993 SEATS   VOTES (MLNS)  PCT OF VOTE</p>
<p> Liberal	    155	174	    4.861	    38.4</p>
<p> Reform		60	 52	    2.451	    19.3</p>
<p> Bloc Quebecois    44	 54	    1.359	    10.7</p>
<p> New Democratic    21	  9	    1.399	    11.0</p>
<p> Conservative	20	  2	    2.393	    18.9</p>
<p>One independent member of Parliament was elected, and five other parties gathered votes but no seats. A total of 12.671 million of 19.161 million registered voters cast ballots, a participation rate of 66.1 percent. The new House of Commons was six seats larger at 301 seats.</p>
<p>The percentages were calculated by Reuters.</p>
